<h2>Communicating the design intent</h2>
<p>A competition model brings building form, façade treatments and spatial relationships into one physical presentation. Selecting the appropriate level of detail helps communicate the proposal without distracting from its central architectural ideas.</p>
<p>For this visitor center, glazing and mesh were part of that discussion. Their representation needed to work with the model’s overall form while making the façade details legible.</p>
